                  <history>
                     <origin>
                        <origDate when-custom="1250/1400" notBefore="1250" notAfter="1400"
                           calendar="#gregorian">s. xiii ex.-xiv ex.</origDate>
                     </origin>
                     <provenance><orgName role="fmo" key="org_439">Oxford, Oxfordshire. The Queen's
                           College</orgName><p>Fol. 56r '7vo'. See A. G. Little, 'Tractatus fratris
                           Thomae de Eccleston', Collection d'Etudes et de Documents VII (1909), pp.
                           xiii-xvii. Evidently the MS. referred to by Bale as being at Queen's
                           College Oxford (see <title>Index Britanniae Scriptorum</title>, pp. 473,
                           378, 437, 238 for arts. 14, 21–23, 27–30 in the table of contents printed
                           by Little). </p></provenance>
                     <provenance type="MLGB3_LaterOwners"><persName role="fmo">Bale</persName>, who
                        also owned the other parts of Phillipps 3119. See Honor McCusker, 'Books and
                        Manuscripts formerly in the Possession of John Bale', <title>The
                           Library</title>, 4th ser., 16 (1935), nos. 48-9, 133, 170-73. Bale's hand
                        occurs on many leaves and a slip inserted after fol. 86 is in his
                        writing.</provenance>
                  </history>
