                  </msContents>
                  <history>
                     <origin>
                        <origDate when-custom="11XX" notBefore="1100" notAfter="1199"
                           calendar="#gregorian">s. xii</origDate>
                     </origin>
                     <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_456">Ramsey,
                           Huntingdonshire. Benedictine Abbey of Saint Mary the Virgin and St
                           Benedict</orgName><p>'Liber Rameseye' (fol. 175v, top, towards right; s.
                           xiv).</p><p> </p></provenance>
                     <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">The life of Abbo by Haymo of Fleury was
                        seen by Bale at Ramsey (<title>Index Britanniae Scriptorum</title> p. 155).
                        This is no doubt <persName role="fmo">Bale's</persName> copy and is bound up
                        with other manuscripts which certainly belonged to him. 'Haymo Floriacensis
                        de vita Abbonis monachi' is no. 77 in the list of Bale's manuscripts (see
                        Honor McCusker, 'Books and Manuscripts formerly in the Possession of John
                        Bale', <title>The Library</title>, 4th ser., 16 (1935), pp. 144–65 at p.
                        153). Compare Ramsey Cat. p. 3611.</provenance>
                  </history>
