                     </objectDesc>
                  </physDesc>
                  <history>
                     <origin>
                        <origDate when-custom="13XX/14XX" notBefore="1300" notAfter="1499"
                           calendar="#gregorian">s. xiv/xv</origDate>
                     </origin>
                     <provenance><orgName role="fmo" key="org_425">Oxford, Oxfordshire. All Souls'
                           College</orgName><p>It seems likely that this MS., which belonged to
                              <persName role="fmo">Bale</persName>, is the one which he saw at All
                           Souls College (<title>Index Britanniae Scriptorum</title> p. 452). No
                           other copy of the shorter chronicle (Inc.: 'Multi nobilis ac pietatis
                           studio') is known. The MS. now ends imperfect at 1177, but a note in the
                           Phillipps cat. says that it went to 18 H. iiii, 'a quaternio being lost
                           at the end'.</p></provenance>
                     <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners"><persName role="fmo">Bale</persName>, who
                        also owned the other parts of Phillipps 3119. See Honor McCusker, 'Books and
                        Manuscripts formerly in the Possession of John Bale', <title>The
                           Library</title>, 4th ser., 16 (1935), no. 27.</provenance>
                  </history>
